# bond.dag — P5 mode/lifecycle DAG (data, not code).
#
# The ONE source of truth for what the executor (bond-xctl) does. Parsed
# IDENTICALLY by:
#   - deploy/p5/bond-xctl        (busybox sh: IFS='|' read; runs the named
#                                 guard/action/verify shell functions)
#   - orchestration/bond_model.py (the P5 CANDIDATE machine: runs the named
#                                 guard/action/verify Python functions)
# so the equivalence proof drives the SAME table the box would run
# (data-equivalence, not a re-implementation). Behaviour changes are
# reviewable diffs to this file, validated in the emulator, shipped
# read-only and atomically mv-swapped.
#
# FORMAT  (7 pipe-delimited fields; '#' comment lines and blanks ignored)
#   intent | from | to | guards | actions | verify | retries | onfail
#     intent   the trigger the CLI/hook/ecod funnels into bond-xctl:
#              `bond-xctl <intent> [arg]`. Level-triggered: the executor
#              derives the CURRENT node from probes every invocation and
#              the action list is idempotent, so an already-satisfied
#              intent is a verify-only no-op (I4 idempotency, I2 self-heal).
#     from     comma-set of nodes this intent applies from (`*`=any).
#     to       the desired node the intent converges toward.
#     guards   comma-list of guard probes; ALL must pass or the edge is
#              refused (logged, no state change). `-` = none.
#     actions  comma-list of actions run in order. `-` = none.
#     verify   post-condition probe (retried); `-` = none.
#     retries  attempts for `verify` before taking `onfail`.
#     onfail   intent to follow when `verify` still fails. `-` = none.
#
# NODES: off · engaged · agg · suspended · suspended_degraded
#   engaged carries the mode fact (lightning|eco) as a side value;
#   suspended / suspended_degraded are OUTCOME nodes (reached only via the
#   `suspend` onfail of a failed engage), never desired targets.
#
# Maps to HANDOVER §2/§4 transitions T1..T11 (see the `# T#` tag per row).
#
# The CLI (bondctl) writes the DESIRED facts first (mode, auto) and, for a
# failed `agg` engage, restores the prior mode — those are CLI duties, NOT edges.
# The executor only walks these edges. `engage` retries=5 is the roaming
# convergence budget (matches the historical 5-iteration engage loop:
# <=4 in-flight roams still converge, >=5 -> suspend).
#
# NODES are {off, engaged, suspended, suspended_degraded}: `rc` (bond on/off)
# is the engaged/off discriminator, `susp` overrides. AGGREGATION is a MODE, not
# a node — an aggregating box is node `engaged` carrying mode ∈ {max, speed}
# (feeder = bond-agg). Exactly one feeder runs, selected by mode:
# `aggdown_if_agg` leads engage/switch/disengage so INV1 (single feeder) holds by
# construction (this closes a latent two-feeder edge the deployed bondctl had on
# the on-during-aggregate and reboot-during-aggregate sequences — a mandatory INV1
# fix, backstopped by watchdog W3).
#
# ONE AGGREGATE INTENT (U17). ADR-003 splits the aggregate mode into `max`
# (stripe everything) and `speed` (fewest/fastest for the offered load). They are
# ONE lifecycle here — same feeder, same listener, same guards, same enrolled
# source set — differing only in the AGG_SCHED fact `build_agg_env` emits into
# agg_env. So there is ONE `agg` row, not one row per mode: a new aggregate
# scheduler adds a row to bond-xctl's AGG_SCHED_TABLE and NOTHING to this file.
# A max<->speed flip is an agg_env byte change -> the existing `agg_env_changed`
# crumb -> `agg_restart`; it walks this same edge, so it needs no new one.
#
# GUARD SPELLING (U6): the aggregate guard is `enough_sources`, NOT the old
# `two_wans`. It always MEANT ">= MIN_AGG_SOURCES live sources" -- an ARITY
# requirement with no upper bound -- and the old spelling read as a 2-WAN
# assumption that the box does not have (it declares FOUR WANs,
# docs/INTENT.md:193). Both parsers resolve it to the one N-generic predicate:
# bond_model.py registers `enough_sources` AND `two_wans` onto
# g_enough_sources_to_aggregate (NG-0 asserts they are identical), and
# bond-xctl run_guard accepts both spellings so a half-upgraded box (new
# bond-xctl, old bond.dag still on disk) resolves the guard rather than
# refusing every aggregate edge.
#
# intent|from|to|guards|actions|verify|retries|onfail
engage|off,engaged,suspended,suspended_degraded|engaged|installed|aggdown_if_agg,rc_on,genconf,eng_enable,eng_restart,ep_local|verify_local|5|suspend
suspend|off,engaged,suspended,suspended_degraded|suspended|-|revert|-|0|-
disengage|off,engaged,suspended,suspended_degraded|off|installed|aggdown_if_agg,rc_off,eng_disable,eng_stop,ep_direct,clear_susp|-|0|-
switch|off,engaged,suspended,suspended_degraded|engaged|installed|aggdown_if_agg,genconf_if_enabled,eng_restart_if_enabled|-|0|-
agg|off,engaged|agg|installed,manual,agg_installed,enough_sources|env_gen,agg_install,eng_stop,agg_enable,agg_restart,mtu_1408,ep_agg|verify_agg|3|agg_revert
agg_revert|off,engaged|engaged|-|agg_stop,agg_disable,mtu_1420,restore_feeder|-|0|-
